# AnnW LanMp — Architecture Gate

When working under `LanMp/` or `docs/lan-mp/`:

## Non-negotiable (ADR-004 / INV-T*)

1. **Turn cursor** (`turns`, `current_co_index`, `cur_player`) advances on Host only via vanilla turn code; Guest applies **only** through `EndTurn` Command fields (`nextPlayerIndex`, `turnsAfter`).
2. **Never** fix desync by adding another Harmony `Prefix` that calls `MannualEndTurn` on Guest to "catch up".
3. All battle `Command` applies go through **`CommandApplyQueue`** (serial). No parallel `CoApply*`.
4. Non-local seats (remote human + all AI) use **one** RemoteWatch path.
5. LAN: do not let `last_human_player.defeated` alone stop the global turn loop.
6. MatchEnd is Host-only and multi-seat; no single-bool fake settlement as the design.
7. Solo / campaign: no LAN turn hooks unless `InLanBattle` / `StartAuthorized`.
8. **INV-VIEW:** In LAN, `last_human_player` means **local FOW/UI viewer**, never the remote human whose turn it is. Do not let vanilla hotseat assignment fight FOWDirty rebinding (main-thread FOW re-entry freeze on Host EndTurn→Guest).
9. Host authoritative EndTurn Accept uses **`SuppressNetworkEmit` only** — never `ApplyingRemoteCommand` (that flag is Guest/replay).
10. **CoroutineObject ≠ Unity:** `yield return null` on `GameController` busy-spins the same `ExecuteContext` (Host EndTurn white-screen / Guest Apply stuck). Waits must use `AnnWCoroutine.NextTick` (`0f`). **CommandApplyQueue / Host Accept must drive bodies through `AnnWCoroutine.SafePump`** (flatten nested `IEnumerator`, map null/`0`/`0f`→NextTick) — never `yield return` vanilla animators straight into CoroutineObject. Boxed `int 0` (vanilla move/attack lerp) must yield one tick — treating it as wait-0s teleports Guest units.
11. **Checksum:** LAN checkpoints are EndTurn `stateHash` over the **attachment payload**. Recapture/`Save_General` drift after Apply must not Strict-pause Guest (Apply is lossy; Host attachment is ADR-001 truth).
12. **Guest Intent in-flight:** Guest may have at most one mutating Intent awaiting Host Command/Nack. No click-spam Accept. Host Accept must `SuppressNetworkEmit` through `HostBroadcastCommand` so Bus cannot emit a twin Command.
13. **INV-ACCEPT:** Board geometry/FOW legality for Guest UnitMoved/DoAction is **Host Accept only** (`ActionLegality` / `IntentAcceptLegalityRules`). Guest gate may block ownership/spent/spectate/in-flight — **never** fail-fast `GetMoveZone`/`CanDoAction` (0.18.2 regression). Host move: `GetMoveZone(false,true,false)` hard miss; DoAction: hard `IsPosInSelectZone` + hard `CanDoAction` FOW under **PreferUnitOwnerFow** (`TARGET_NOT_VISIBLE` / DETECTED≠SEEN — no soft-pass). Guest UX: INV-VIEW transpile + post-attach `RefreshLocalVision` (vision + combat UX caches). Always bind Intent extras before CanDoAction.
14. **Seat defeat / Surrender:** `player.defeated` stamps from attachment **independent of eco ResourceApplyMode** (`ApplySeatDefeatFlags` + `TriggerPlayerDefeat`). Surrender ≠ EndGame; MatchEnd settlement uses vanilla `proc_EndGame` (`AllowVanillaEndGameUi`), never custom IMGUI.
15. **CastSkill presentation:** Guest `DoActionAni` + `PresentationSkipActionCell` (no DoActionCell re-sim). Host Command must carry `hasTarget`/tile/extras — never default aim (0,0). Ownership skills need `ownerIndex`→`ConvertUnitOwnerShip` (LoadOb does not OnEffectStart).

## Process

- Architectural failures (split operators, double EndTurn, Host-defeat kills match) → change `TurnAuthority` / `CommandApplyQueue` / MatchEnd — **not** a one-off Prefix.
- Feature work (Guest AutoCmd, etc.) waits until P0 turn authority acceptance criteria pass.
- Declare which INV-T* a change upholds in the PR/commit message or reply.
